Package: tind-extensions
Version: 0.1.1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Morten <morten@servr.no>
Section: gnome
Priority: optional
Depends: gnome-shell (>= 48), libglib2.0-bin
Installed-Size: 1
Description: Tind GNOME Shell extensions: System Monitor and Multi Monitor Bar
 Two third-party GNOME Shell extensions that Tind enables by default, shipped
 system-wide (both GPL-2.0-or-later):
 .
  * System Monitor (system-monitor-panel@naimur) by naimur900:
    CPU, memory, disk, network and temperature in the top bar.
    https://github.com/naimur900/system-monitor-panel-gnome
  * Multi Monitor Bar (multi-monitors-bar@frederykabryan) by Frederyk Abryan,
    a fork of Multi Monitors by spin83: top bar on every monitor.
    https://github.com/FrederykAbryan/multi-monitors-bar_fapv2
 .
 Which extensions are enabled is set in tind-branding's dconf defaults.
 Both extensions list GNOME Shell 48 (Debian 13) as supported.
